1. ENCAPSULATION: Private variables in Product.java (id, name, price, quantity) accessed via public getters/setters.
2. INHERITANCE: Food extends Product (Single); PerishableFood extends Food (Multi-level).
3. POLYMORPHISM: getDisplayInfo() is overridden in Food and PerishableFood.
4. ABSTRACTION: Product is an abstract class with an abstract method getDisplayInfo().
5. COMPOSITION: InventoryManager has an ArrayList of Product objects.
6. RESPONSIBILITIES: InventoryManager handles logic (sellProduct, restockProduct), while Main handles the menu loop.
7.NON-STATIC METHODS:InventoryManager.java: registerNewProduct(), displayReceipt(), sellProduct(), Inventory.java: addProduct(), viewProducts(), findProductById()
8.CLASSES:
Product.java: Abstract base class for all products
Food.java: Concrete class representing food items
 PerishableFood.java: Concrete class representing perishable food items
 InventoryManager.java: Service class managing inventory operations
 Inventory.java: Utility class for product list management
 transactions.java: Model class for tracking sales transactions
 Main.java: Entry point class for the application
